格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"专为 DeepSeek API 打造的实时用量 / 费用 / 余额计量插件 —— 在聊天输入框旁直接看到 tokens、花费与真实余额。","id":"gh:1336911755","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-usage-meter-harness","slug":"faith1688/dsh-usage-meter-harness","topics":["dsh-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"专为 DeepSeek API 打造的实时用量 / 费用 / 余额计量插件 —— 在聊天输入框旁直接看到 tokens、花费与真实余额。"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-usage-meter-harness"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 简体中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"A real-time usage / cost / balance meter plugin for **DeepSeek Harness (DSH)**.\nSee tokens, spending"},{"id":"p4s2","text":" and real wallet balance right next to the chat input — for\nthe official DeepSeek models **and** any"},{"id":"p4s3","text":" custom model registered in DSH."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"> Prerequisite (methods 1 & 2): the DSH CLI itself runs on pnpm — install it once per machine:\n> `np"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"m install -g pnpm` (or `corepack enable`), then verify with `pnpm --version`."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Pick one of the three methods. **Methods 1 and 2 need pnpm** (a one-time machine\nsetup used by the D"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"SH CLI itself): `npm install -g pnpm` or `corepack enable`."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"### Method 1 — npm registry via DSH CLI (needs pnpm)"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"(`--verbose` shows the install progress; drop it if you prefer a quiet install.\n`@latest` explicitly"},{"id":"p10s2","text":" requests the newest release — always install this way.)"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"### Method 2 — GitHub via DSH CLI (needs pnpm)"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"(`--verbose` shows the install progress. `#main` always installs the latest\nmain branch — the newest"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"e` shows the install progress. `#main` always installs the latest\nmain branch — the newest release.)"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"### Method 3 — one-line installer, no pnpm (recommended)"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"One command: installs into the DSH web profile and registers the bundle (idempotent).\n(`@latest` exp"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"licitly requests the newest release — always install this way.)"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Prefer not to use npx? The same logic ships as scripts in the repo:"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Windows (cmd):"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Linux / macOS:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"The script does everything for you: `cd` into the DSH web profile, installs the\npackage with visible"},{"id":"p22s2","text":" progress, and registers the bundle in `dsh.profile.bundles`\n(idempotent — safe to re-run after upgr"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"ess, and registers the bundle in `dsh.profile.bundles`\n(idempotent — safe to re-run after upgrades)."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"> Note: Method 3 uses plain `npm` and does **not** do pnpm coordination. If your\n> profile is manage"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"d with pnpm (the default for `dsh plugin`), prefer Method 1."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"After any method: **restart `dsh web`**."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"## Updating"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"Two cases — pick the right one:"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"**Fresh install (never had the plugin), or the `npx` method:** just run the\ninstall command; it alwa"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"ys fetches the latest release."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"**Upgrading an existing install (plugin already present):** the profile's\n`package.json` / `pnpm-loc"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"k.yaml` may be pinned to an old version, and a bare\n`add` can be skipped by pnpm as \"already satisfi"},{"id":"p28s3","text":"ed\". **Always ask for the new\nversion explicitly:**"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"or, from inside the profile directory (`~/.dsh/profiles/web`):"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"(You may also pin an exact version, e.g. `...@1.0.28`.)"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"> **Marketplace update failed?** If it reports *\"targeted vX but installed vY; the\n> previous versio"},{"id":"p33s2","text":"n was restored automatically\"*, that is pnpm's **new-release\n> cooldown** (`minimumReleaseAge` — a f"},{"id":"p33s3","text":"reshly published version is skipped for\n> roughly 24h). Your install is not broken and nothing in yo"},{"id":"p33s4","text":"ur config or data was\n> touched. **Wait 24 hours** and click update again, or upgrade right away wit"},{"id":"p33s5","text":"h the\n> `npx` command below (or add this package name, without a version, to\n> `minimumReleaseAgeExc"},{"id":"p33s6","text":"lude` in your profile's `pnpm-workspace.yaml`)."},{"id":"p34s1","text":"**If your `package.json` binds the plugin via a `file:` path or a pin that `add`\nwon't override** (y"},{"id":"p34s2","text":"ou see `Already up to date` / `downloaded 0`), use the\none-line installer instead — it always reques"},{"id":"p34s3","text":"ts `@latest`, which rewrites the\nbinding to `^<latest>` and upgrades in a single command:"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"(Re-running this same command is the permanent update path: it is idempotent\nand upgrades regardless"},{"id":"p36s2","text":" of whether you currently bind via `file:`, a pin, or `^`.)"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"After updating: **restart `dsh web`** (or reload the browser page). Note that\nrestarting alone never"},{"id":"p37s2","text":" fetches a new version — it only reloads what is already\nin `node_modules`."},{"id":"p38s1","text":"**Why this never duplicates the mount entry and never touches your config:**"},{"id":"p39s1","text":"- The mount entry lives **inside the package** (`cordis.patch.yml`, the\n`dsh.bundle` mechanism). Eve"},{"id":"p39s2","text":"ry release ships its own complete entry; DSH reads\nit from the installed package at startup — instal"},{"id":"p39s3","text":"ling a newer package\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p40s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p41s1","text":"### Conversation usage card (next to the chat input)"},{"id":"p42s1","text":"| Feature | Description |"},{"id":"p43s1","text":"| Live cost | Session cost in CNY or USD, updated every step |\n| Token breakdown | Input (miss) / ca"},{"id":"p43s2","text":"che hit / cache write / output |\n| Turn usage panel | Per-turn subtotals with unit prices tagged pea"},{"id":"p43s3","text":"k/off-peak |\n| Token speed | Live tokens/s while streaming; resets cleanly when output stops or tool"},{"id":"p43s4","text":"s run |\n| Cache hit rate | Share of cached tokens for the session |\n| Account balance | Real DeepSee"},{"id":"p43s5","text":"k wallet balance; local-ledger estimate for other providers |\n| Budget & remaining | Set a budget, s"},{"id":"p43s6","text":"ee used / remaining / over-budget |"},{"id":"p44s1","text":"### Billing engine"},{"id":"p45s1","text":"| Feature | Description |"},{"id":"p46s1","text":"| 6 billing templates | Basic · Cache hit/miss · Peak/off-peak (DeepSeek official hours) · Cache wri"},{"id":"p46s2","text":"te+hit · Combined input+output · Batch half price |\n| Custom price rows | Up to 4 user-defined rows;"},{"id":"p46s3","text":" the popup mirrors your setup verbatim |\n| Peak/off-peak billing | Beijing-time weekday + hour windo"},{"id":"p46s4","text":"ws, cross-midnight supported; each request is billed by its start time |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p47s1","text":"## Compatibility"},{"id":"p48s1","text":"- Node.js ≥ 22.\n- Peer versions track the supported DSH releases (see `package.json`); updating\nDSH "},{"id":"p48s2","text":"does not break the plugin, and it never modifies your other plugins."},{"id":"p49s1","text":"## Privacy"},{"id":"p50s1","text":"- The plugin makes **no telemetry and no analytics calls**.\n- Network requests are limited to four o"},{"id":"p50s2","text":"ptional ones, all initiated by you: querying the\n**official DeepSeek balance API** with the API key "},{"id":"p50s3","text":"you configure yourself, fetching a\npublic USD→CNY exchange rate, fetching the official pricing page "},{"id":"p50s4","text":"during a one-click\nprice sync, and — only when rule parsing fails — sending that page's content to t"},{"id":"p50s5","text":"he\nDeepSeek API with your global key for extraction. Nothing else leaves your machine.\n- The source "},{"id":"p50s6","text":"is MIT-licensed and fully readable on GitHub."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
